  "worked_solution": "We are given the units $\\frac{\\text{hours}}{\\text{day}},$ and we want to convert this into $\\frac{\\text{min}}{\\text{week}}.$ We're converting two units instead of just one, so we're going to have to multiply by two conversion factors:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{hours}}{\\text{day}}\\cdot \\,\\frac{?}{?}\\cdot \\,\\frac{?}{?}=\\frac{\\text{min}}{\\text{week}}\n$$\n\nOne of the conversion factors should change $\\text{hours}$ to $\\text{min}.$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{hours}}}{\\text{day}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{min}}{\\cancel{\\text{hour}}}\\cdot \\,\\frac{?}{?}=\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{s}}\n$$\n\nThe other conversion factor should change $\\text{day}$ into $\\text{week}.$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{hours}}}{\\cancel{\\text{day}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{min}}{\\cancel{\\text{hour}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{\\text{days}}}{\\text{week}}=\\frac{\\text{min}}{\\text{week}}\n$$\n\nSo, our conversion formula is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{hours}}{\\text{day}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{min}}{\\text{hour}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{days}}{\\text{week}}=\\frac{\\text{min}}{\\text{week}}.\n$$\n\nNow that we have our conversion formula, we need to determine the correct numbers to use, and apply it.\n\n- The rate given in the problem statement is $0.5\\,\\frac{\\text{hours}}{\\text{day}}.$\n\n- There are $60$ minutes per hour.\n\n- There are $7$ days per week.\n\nApplying our conversion formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.5\\,\\frac{\\text{hours}}{\\text{day}} & =0.5\\,\\frac{\\text{hours}}{\\text{day}}\\cdot 60\\,\\frac{\\text{min}}{\\text{hour}}\\cdot 7\\,\\frac{\\text{days}}{\\text{week}} \\\\  & =(0.5\\cdot 60\\cdot 7)\\,\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{hours}}}{\\cancel{\\text{day}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{min}}{\\cancel{\\text{hour}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{\\text{days}}}{\\text{week}} \\\\  & =210\\,\\frac{\\text{min}}{\\text{week}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, Lewis studies at a rate of $210\\,\\text{min/week}.$",
